{"baseRefName":"beta","body":"## What\n\n`resources/views/livewire/partials/unit-tree-picker.blade.php` builds the whole org tree in PHP (string concatenation) and embeds every unit as inline JSON. On the dev database (834 units) that is **≈494 KB of HTML per render** — and it was included **unconditionally**:\n\n| page | modals | cost per render |\n|---|---|---|\n| `users.index` | 1 (`unitModal`) | ≈494 KB, even while the modal is closed |\n| `kargozini/person` | 2 (`filterUnitModal`, `unitModal`) | ≈988 KB, even with both modals closed |\n\nMaryUI's `<x-modal>` renders its slot unconditionally (only `open` is entangled), so a closed modal saved zero bytes. Every keystroke, every page change and every search on those two pages paid for a tree nobody was looking at.\n\nEach include site now sits behind the flag of the modal it belongs to:\n\n- `resources/views/livewire/users/index.blade.php` → `@if ($unitModal)`\n- `resources/views/livewire/kargozini/person.blade.php` → `@if ($filterUnitModal)` and `@if ($unitModal)` (the two modals stay independent)\n- `resources/views/livewire/partials/unit-tree-picker.blade.php` → a header line so the next consumer knows it must include it inside an `@if`\n\nOpening a modal is **already** a round trip (`wire:click=\"$set('unitModal', true)\"`), so the tree is built exactly when it becomes visible — **no extra request** is added; the cost only moves to the moment the user opens the picker.\n\n## What is NOT changed\n\n- The scope contract (#849 / #1040) is untouched: `@if` changes **when** the tree renders, not **which** units it contains. An empty scope still renders an empty tree, never the whole organization.\n- `allUnitsTree()` stays the same `#[Computed]` (#1040).\n- `with()` on `kargozini/person` stays as it is — moving `$units` to a computed/lazy source is a **separate issue**.\n- No API, migration, config or dependency change.\n\n## Manual check of the FIRST modal opening (Alpine init on the morphed-in node)\n\nChecked by hand in the browser (Playwright / Chromium against the e2e stack) on **both** pages, opening each modal for the **first** time:\n\n- The tree is **absent from the DOM while the modal is closed** and appears with the modal.\n- **Alpine IS initialised on the freshly morphed-in node**: the new node carries Alpine's data stack (`_x_dataStack`), `Alpine.$data(node)` resolves, and the picker's own `x-model=\"search\"` + `$watch('search', …)` react to typing inside that new node (the matched unit gets `bg-warning/25`).\n- **Clicking a node works end to end**: the picker's `toggle()` writes the Livewire model, the round trip completes, and the form shows the selected-unit chip.\n- On `kargozini/person` each modal was opened on its own first time: the filter picker binds `filter_u_id`, the form picker binds `u_id`, and neither one brings the other's tree.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `#849: user table, unit picker and person search are unit-scoped` — the scope assertions now run in the **open**-modal state (on a closed modal they would be vacuously true); the closed state additionally asserts that no tree and no inline unit JSON are in the DOM.\n- `#849: an empty scope renders nobody, not everybody` — the modal is opened before the tree assertions, so \"empty scope ⇒ empty tree, not the whole org\" is a real assertion again.\n- `PersonLivewireTest::test_filter_unit_name_does_not_leak_an_out_of_scope_unit` — the filter modal is opened before the assertion, for the same reason.\n- `PersonLivewireTest::test_empty_scope_renders_no_unit_name_at_all` — both modals are opened, so the assertion is about a rendered (empty) tree.\n- **New** `#1171: the unit tree renders only while the modal is open` — closed ⇒ no tree, open ⇒ the scoped tree, closed again ⇒ the tree is dropped.\n- **New** `#1171: a 200-unit tree does not reach the closed page` — a synthetic 200-unit hierarchy: the closed page must not grow at all when the org tree grows, while the open page carries the tree (tens of KB).\n- **New** `test_the_two_unit_pickers_render_only_inside_their_own_modal` — on `kargozini.person` both modals closed ⇒ no tree; opening one brings only its own tree (proved through the model each picker binds to).\n\nAll four changed/added tests were verified to **fail against the old Blade code** and pass against the new one.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `composer test` (full suite) | 2541 passed, 2 risky (pre-existing, unrelated file), 0 failed |\n| `vendor/bin/phpstan analyse --no-progress` | no errors — `phpstan-baseline.neon` unchanged (0 new entries) |\n| `vendor/bin/pint --test` | passed |\n| `scripts/check-app-key-leak.php` | OK |\n| `scripts/find-dead-test-files.php` | OK |\n\n`kargozini/person.blade.php` also carries the one-line phpdoc indent fix that the repo's pre-commit hook applies to that file.\n\nCloses #1171\n","headRefName":"perf/1171-unit-tree-picker-render-on-open","headRepositoryOwner":{"id":"U_kgDOE43R5Q","name":"Sydney","login":"haileen5"},"number":1205,"state":"OPEN","title":"perf: build the unit tree only while its modal is open (#1171)","url":"https://github.com/asgarimehdi/h-dashboard/pull/1205"}
